<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Completion" id="Completion">

    <web-summary>
        Enable %tool_name% shell completion for bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell to complete commands, flags and flag
        values such as --scope.
    </web-summary>

    <p>
        %tool_name% can complete commands, flags and flag values (such as <code>--scope</code>) when you press
        <shortcut>Tab</shortcut>.
    </p>

    <note>
        Running <code>%tool_call% completion &lt;shell&gt;</code> only prints the completion script on the standard
        output.
    </note>

    <chapter title="Enable completion" id="completion_chapter-enable">
        <p>Supported shells are bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell.</p>

        <tabs>
            <tab title="Bash">
                <p>Add this line to <path>~/.bashrc</path>:</p>
                <code-block lang="bash"><![CDATA[
source <(%tool_call% completion bash)
]]></code-block>
                <p>Completion for bash requires the <code>bash-completion</code> package.</p>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Zsh">
                <p>Add these lines to <path>~/.zshrc</path>:</p>
                <code-block lang="bash"><![CDATA[
autoload -U compinit && compinit
source <(%tool_call% completion zsh)
]]></code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Fish">
                <p>Add this line to <path>~/.config/fish/config.fish</path>:</p>
                <code-block lang="shell"><![CDATA[
%tool_call% completion fish | source
]]></code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="PowerShell">
                <p>Open your profile with <code>notepad $PROFILE</code> and add this line:</p>
                <code-block lang="powershell"><![CDATA[
%tool_call% completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
]]></code-block>
                <p>
                    If the profile file does not exist yet, create it first with
                    <code>New-Item -ItemType File -Force $PROFILE</code>.
                </p>
            </tab>
        </tabs>

        <p>
            Next, open a new terminal, then type <code>%tool_call% </code> followed by <shortcut>Tab</shortcut>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

</topic>
